<title>USA: Food Lion plans $300 mln debt offering.</title>
<headline>Food Lion plans $300 mln debt offering.</headline>
<dateline>SALISBURY, N.C. 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food Lion Inc said Tuesday it plans to issue up to $300 million in debt securities, which will be used to retire certain indebtedness and extend the average maturity of its outstanding debt from two years to twelve years.</p>
<p>The company said Salomon Brothers Inc and NationsBanc Capital Markets Inc will  manage the offering.</p>
<p>The Food Lion supermarket chain encompassses  more than 1,200 stores in 14 states.</p>
</text>
